Z||000039||Songman||06-28-2001||12:09 AM||||Heather,<P>No one asked my opinion, but I do know one thing... You never know someone until you have lived with them 24 hours a day. And sometimes not even then. <P>My family and my good Baptist upbringing taught me to abstain until marriage. But I always said that I would live with someone before marrying them. I have lived with a few and ended up glad I did because no marriage came of it for me to have to buy my way out of.. The one time I did marry, I didn't live with her first. Two months later I was gone. Luckily, my lawyer was better than hers so it didn't cost me all that much.. but she did try!<P>I think you can maintain your character and morals while still living with someone. But in the end it is no one's choice to make but yours... Good luck to you two...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
